a newly released video recorded by the  u.s navy personnel two years ago  shows an unknown sphere that followed a  navy warship before  disappearing into the ocean the video  provides the latest glimpse into an  ongoing pentagon investigation  into ufos i-team reporter george knapp  unveils details about the encounter  earlier on today on our mystery wire  website george  ryan you know uh ufos are in the air if  i'm here in the studio something's going  on  now this video was made public today by  our colleague filmmaker jeremy corbell  with analysis and background on mystery  wire  the unknown object was one of several  that essentially surrounded the navy  warship  multiple times over three days four  other navy ships had similar encounters  over a period of several days in july  2019  at least five u.s navy warships based in  san diego  were swarmed by drone-like objects of  unknown origin  one of those ships the uss omaha was on  maneuvers more than 100 miles directly  west of san diego  and beyond the channel islands one of  the omaha's central missions is  surveillance so it's packed  with cutting edge technology and sensors  but it appears the omaha was itself  under surveillance  this video was recorded inside the  omaha's command center  just before 11 pm on july 15. the image  on the screen shows a six foot in  diameter sphere that  traveled alongside the omaha for about  an hour  it was pitch black outside so the image  was obtained via a thermal sensor  personnel in the command center made  multiple recordings of what was on the  screen  at precisely 11 p.m the unidentified  spear  seemingly vanished into the ocean  splashed when they say splash splash  that doesn't mean there was a physical  splash  that means this object went into the  water or they suspect  it did filmmaker jeremy corbell obtained  the video from sources he declines to  identify  in april corbell and mystery wire  released a series of other  startling images that are included in a  briefing presentation  prepared by the uap task force a unit  created by congress last year  to collect ufo-related images and  information  for a comprehensive report due next  month one  image from the uap task force is a  freeze frame slide  of the sphere seen beside the omaha the  pentagon has confirmed that image was  captured by navy personnel  the task force considers it to be a  genuine unknown  other journalists have confirmed that  multiple navy ships in the same vicinity  were buzzed by unknown objects during  the same time  frame july 2019 corbell says as many as  14 of the spheres  surrounded the omaha and were detected  on sensors  on and off during three perplexing days  at sea  the omaha's advanced sensors could not  maintain a lock on the spheres  as they approached the ship or when they  departed they never found  where these things came from or went to  so they don't know where they're  launching from or going from i mean  maybe it's the water because that's what  we're seeing one do  mark bearing voices on the video  confirmed the omaha launched an  immediate search using all of its  high-tech resources but when the  spear vanished from the screen it also  vanished from the omaha's radar and  sonar  no wreckage was found on the surface  the uap task force briefing is a  classified document but the images  contained in that briefing  are not classified that distinction was  made so the task force could use images  like this to brief other military and  intelligence officials  about the ufo mystery simply put the  navy does not know what these things are  they are still considered to be unknown
 

